 **Hibernate check** (`crates/centurion-helpers/src/hibernate.rs`, `gui/src/sleeppage.cpp`): `tune-profile-helper {"op":"hibernate_check"}` as the user (`userhelper`), read-only. Reads `/proc/meminfo`, `/proc/swaps` (zram excluded from the swap total), `/proc/cmdline` (`resume=`), `/sys/firmware/efi/efivars/HibernateLocation-8cf2644b-…`, `/sys/kernel/security/lockdown` (the bracketed mode), `/sys/power/state`, and for a device-mapper swap `/sys/block/dm-N/dm/{name,uuid}` (`CRYPT-LUKS…` / other `CRYPT-…` = plain). `analyse` gives codes (`no_disk_state`, `lockdown`, `no_swap`, `swap_small`, `no_resume`, `swap_plain_crypt`, `swap_luks`, `ready`); the GUI words them.
 
-**Memory test** (`gui/src/memtest.cpp` logic + `tests/memtest_test.cpp`, `gui/src/memtestbox.cpp`, `memory_spd.rs::aod_snapshot`): Health → Curve stability. The GUI runs `stressapptest -M <MiB> -s <s>` (preferred) or `memtester <MiB>M` (no loop count; terminated at the deadline, which is its normal end) as the user. Size = the chosen share of `MemAvailable`; for memtester also at most `RLIMIT_MEMLOCK` (below 64 MiB it does not start and says how to raise the limit). Errors: memtester `FAILURE` lines and exit bits 0x02/0x04; stressapptest `Hardware Error:` lines, its `Found N hardware incidents` and `Status: PASS/FAIL`; plus `mce` events from `CurvePage::onFault` during the run. Verdict pass / fail / incomplete (stopped, crashed, no status line); an error found is a failure however the run ended. Before the run `tune-profile-helper {"op":"mem_snapshot"}` (any user, read-only) decodes the world-readable `AodSetupRpl` efivar on the mapped model/BIOS (`aod_supported`): `speed_mts`, `manual` (fields with mode 1) and `pending` (`/run/centurion/aod-pending` exists: written this boot). Results: `$XDG_STATE_HOME/centurion/memtest.json`, JSON array, newest 50.
+**Memory test** (`gui/src/memtest.cpp` logic + `tests/memtest_test.cpp`, `gui/src/memtestbox.cpp`, `memory_spd.rs::aod_snapshot`): Health → Curve stability. The GUI runs `stressapptest -M <MiB> -s <s>` (preferred) or `memtester <MiB>M` (no loop count; terminated at the deadline, which is its normal end) as the user. Size = the chosen share of `MemAvailable`; for memtester also at most `RLIMIT_MEMLOCK` (below 64 MiB it does not start and says how to raise the limit). Errors: memtester `FAILURE` lines and exit bits 0x02/0x04; stressapptest `Hardware Error:` lines, its `Found N hardware incidents` and `Status: PASS/FAIL`; plus `mce` events from `CurvePage::onFault` during the run. Verdict pass / fail / incomplete (stopped, crashed, no status line); an error found is a failure however the run ended. Before the run `tune-profile-helper {"op":"mem_snapshot"}` (any user, read-only) decodes the world-readable `AodSetupRpl` efivar on the mapped model/BIOS (`aod_supported`): `speed_mts`, `manual` (fields with mode 1) and `pending` (`/run/centurion/aod-pending` exists: written this boot). The verdict is decided 3 s after the tool exits (proc stays set and Start stays disabled), so an `mce` logged by the failure that ended the run, which reaches `onFault` ~1.5 s later through the HealthTab debounce, still counts. When `/dev/kmsg` cannot be opened HealthTab polls every `POLL_ROOT_MS` (5 min) and tells `CurvePage::setKernelLog(false)`; both test boxes then show a muted note that kernel events are not counted, and each result gets `"kernel_log": false` (key omitted when the log is live). Results: `$XDG_STATE_HOME/centurion/memtest.json`, JSON array, newest 50.
 
 **Boot history and pstore** (`crates/centurion-helpers/src/boothist.rs`, `pstore.rs`, `gui/src/bootpage.cpp`): `health-reader {"op":"boots"}` (read-only, same silent polkit action as the scan) returns `boothist::build` over `exposure.json`, `oc-journal.jsonl` and `pstore::list`. A boot is `clean` (closed by centurion-boot-guard), `unclean` (`on_boot` found it open), `running` (current) or `unknown` (left open, the guard did not run). `curves` is the ordered, de-duplicated state list per journal kind; an empty object means stock or older than the journal's rotation. A pstore record is attributed to the unclean boot whose lifetime (start to the next boot's start) contains its time, else the nearest within 24 h, else left unattributed. `previous_unclean` (the boot before the current one, when it is unclean) feeds the band in `HealthTab`; the GUI reads that once ~4 s after start and when the page is shown, never periodically. The last 30 kernel-log lines of an unclean boot are taken by the GUI from its own `kernel.log` (`boot=<first 8 of boot_id> seq=` tag); the helper does not know the user's home. pstore sources: `/sys/fs/pstore`, `/var/lib/systemd/pstore` (up to 3 directory levels), and the archive; files are opened `O_NOFOLLOW`, must be regular, are read up to 1 MiB, clipped to the last 12 KiB and passed through `health::scrub`. `tune-helper {"op":"pstore_clear"}` takes nothing from the request: for every file in `/sys/fs/pstore` it writes the scrubbed text to `/var/lib/centurion/pstore/<crash time>-<name>.txt` (`write_root_file`, 0644) and only then `unlink`s the pstore file (a record over 1 MiB, the read limit, stays in place and is reported) (the kernel frees the EFI variable; EFI variables are never touched directly), one `wlog` line per removal; archive files beyond the newest 30 are pruned. The GUI confirms first; the op is not in `PROFILE_OPS`.
 
 **Ryzen limit reasons** (`crates/centurion-helpers/src/pmtable.rs`): `ryzen-co-helper monitor_stream` with `"limits": true` adds the PM table head from `/sys/kernel/ryzen_smu_drv/pm_table`. Desktop-derived tables (version family 0x24 / 0x38 / 0x54 / 0x62): PPT, TDC, THM, EDC at f32 indices 0/1, 2/3, 4/5, 8/9. Mobile APUs (0x37 / 0x40 / 0x45 / 0x4C / 0x5D / 0x65): STAPM, PPT fast / slow, TDC, EDC, THM at 0/1, 2/3, 4/5, 8/9, 12/13, 16/17. Every limit and value must be physically plausible, otherwise nothing is shown ("layout not recognised" + version). ≥ 95 % of a limit counts as binding; the tab sums seconds per limit since the monitor started. Read-only.
 
-**GPU test** (`crates/centurion-gpustress`, `gui/src/gpustress.cpp` logic + `tests/gpustress_test.cpp`, `gui/src/gpustressbox.cpp`; spec `docs/GPUSTRESS.md`): Health → Curve stability. Vendor-neutral Vulkan 1.1 compute, run as the user; the tool never touches clocks or curves, it loads the GPU while the user's curve is in effect. `ash` loads `libvulkan.so.1` at run time (none → `init_failed`); the WGSL shaders in `shaders/` are compiled to SPIR-V by `naga` in `build.rs`. `centurion-gpustress list` prints the devices (PCI address via `VK_EXT_pci_bus_info`, else a unique vendor/device match in sysfs; CPU implementations as `"type":"cpu"`, hidden by the GUI); `vram --device <pci> --percent 10..95 --seconds <s>` and `core --device <pci> --seconds <s>` print JSON lines `start` / `progress` / `error` / `end` (16 error lines per pass, 200 per run; exit 0 pass, 1 errors, 2 device lost, 3 init failure, 4 stopped by SIGTERM/SIGINT). VRAM: chunks of at most 256 MiB from the `DEVICE_LOCAL` heap (share of the `VK_EXT_memory_budget` budget, keeping 256 MiB free), one fenced submission per chunk and dispatch (a fence not signalled within 10 s is a hung GPU: `device_lost`, exit 2); patterns addr / walk1 / walk0 / solid / random are a stateless function of (pattern, global word index, pass), so the check recomputes the expected word and keeps no copy. Core: 1 Mi invocations of dependent f32 FMA + integer mixing, the first two runs must agree and become the reference, every later run is compared with it on the GPU; one dispatch is calibrated to about 100 ms and the seed (new reference pair, recalibration) changes every 60 s. Build feature `fault-inject` (tests only) corrupts one word after the write of pass 3 / disturbs one invocation. The GUI follows the Memory test: verdict pass / fail / incomplete, `xid` (not 45 / 154) and `amdgpu` events from `CurvePage::onFault` count as faults, the run is killed `seconds + 120` s after start, the verdict is decided 3 s after the tool exits so the kernel events the failure caused (delayed by the Monitor's debounce) still count, and it is not offered while an NVIDIA dGPU is on the bus but unusable. Results: `$XDG_STATE_HOME/centurion/gpustress.json`, JSON array, newest 50, with the GPU curve state in effect at start.
